---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "~/data/site";

const colophon = [
  ["Framework", "Astro, static output"],
  ["Type", "Instrument Serif · IBM Plex Mono, self-hosted"],
  ["Styling", "Tailwind, hand-written tokens"],
  ["Data", "GitHub REST API, read at build time"],
  ["Hosting", "GitHub Pages"],
  ["Analytics", "None"],
];
---

<Base
  current="about"
  title="About"
  description={`About ${site.name} — a developer in ${site.location} writing small tools in Python.`}
>
  <section class="pb-14 pt-20 sm:pt-28">
    <h1 class="font-display text-[clamp(2.75rem,9vw,4.5rem)] leading-[0.9] tracking-tight">
      About
    </h1>
  </section>

  {/* Rule spans the full measure so it lines up with the section rules below;
      the prose inside keeps a readable 62ch. */}
  <div class="border-t border-foreground pt-8">
    <div class="max-w-[62ch] space-y-6 text-[0.875rem] leading-[1.75]">
    <p>
      I'm {site.name}. I live in {site.location} and I write mostly Python.
    </p>

    <p>
      Most of my public code comes from one place. My school ran its
      substitution plan through DSBmobile — an app with no public API and no
      apparent interest in having one. <a
        href="https://github.com/timhlzwrt/dsbix"
        class="underline decoration-rule underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-accent-strong hover:decoration-accent-strong"
        >dsbix</a
      > began as a way to read it anyway. It's a rework of nerrixde's DSBApi, and
      it has since been translated to JavaScript, wrapped in an HTTP service and
      pushed to PyPI, which is considerably more attention than the original
      problem deserved.
    </p>

    <p>
      That school is behind me now, and so, largely, is the project. Because
      every school configures DSBmobile differently, the field mapping is
      approximately correct at best — the README says so plainly. I've left it
      up because people still install it, and because taking down working code
      is rude. If it breaks for you, <a
        href="mailto:help@tjh.li"
        class="underline decoration-rule underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-accent-strong hover:decoration-accent-strong"
        >help@tjh.li</a
      > still works.
    </p>

    {/*
      A "Now" section goes well here — what you're working on, studying, or
      reading, in two or three sentences. It's the one part of this page I
      couldn't write without inventing things about you, so I've left it to
      you. Uncomment and fill in:

      <h2 class="label !text-foreground pt-4">Now</h2>
      <p>...</p>
    */}
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="colophon-heading">
    <h2 id="colophon-heading" class="label border-b border-foreground pb-2 !text-foreground">
      Colophon
    </h2>
    <dl class="mt-1">
      {
        colophon.map(([term, value]) => (
          <div class="grid grid-cols-[7.5rem_1fr] gap-x-4 border-b border-rule py-3 text-[0.8125rem] sm:grid-cols-[10rem_1fr]">
            <dt class="label pt-[0.2rem]">{term}</dt>
            <dd class="text-muted-foreground">{value}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
    <h2 id="contact-heading" class="label border-b border-foreground pb-2 !text-foreground">
      Contact
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-[54ch] text-[0.875rem] leading-relaxed">
      <a
        href={`mailto:${site.email}`}
        class="underline decoration-rule underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-accent-strong hover:decoration-accent-strong"
        >{site.email}</a
      > is the fastest way to reach me. Everything else is on the <a
        href="/"
        class="underline decoration-rule underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-accent-strong hover:decoration-accent-strong"
        >index</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
